items.text:
Recruiter here - do they know what you're currently making?  I would tell them you are extremely excited for the position and are happy we are at the offer stage, that you had targeted 50k base / 80k OTE for this position (assuming you didn't tell them anything that contradicts this - THIS IS KEY - you don't want to be seen as someone moving the goal posts), and do they have any room to get you closer to your goal.  This is basically signalling that you would take a 45k base, which is a step up.  Worst case they just say no, but negotiating as a BDR is not a bad trait as long as you handle it tactfully.

&amp;#x200B;

The other thing is have they shown you your comp plan and how you get to the OTE #'s?  I would want to fully understand that before accepting anything.
